          "title": "You'll want to know: خدع",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "خدع — khadaʿa — \"to deceive, to trick\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "خدع الثعلب الغراب في الحكاية. khadaʿa ath-thaʿlab al-ghurāb fī al-ḥikāya. The fox tricked the crow in the tale."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Present: يخدع, yakhdaʿ."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A trick is خدعة."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "خدع (khadaʿa) is built on the native Arabic root kh-d-ʿ (Lane), \"to hide a thing; to deceive\"; khidʿa is a ruse."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
